ned by PNC posts and customary/administrative authorities, with diamond-site disputes and banditry the main security issues. Not verified with fresh sources in this run (web search budget exhausted).","unit":"CD8208-lupatapata","run_id":"drc-swarm-1","presence":[{"entity_id":"cod-fardc","role":"present"}]}],"sources":{},"units":{"CD8208-lupatapata":"Lupatapata is a rural territory of Kasai-Oriental bordering Mbuji-Mayi, made up of the Tshishimbi and Mukumbi sectors. No armed group is known to hold territory there; the Kamuina Nsapu insurgency of 2016-2017 was centred in Kasai-Central and Kasai and largely spared this area. State authority is exercised by the PNC (territorial and sub-commissariats) and local administration, with FARDC and ANR present in the provincial hinterland; insecurity consists of banditry, land/customary disputes and incidents at artisanal diamond sites. Peri-urban neighbourhoods attached to Mbuji-Mayi (Cibombo, Mulenda) are policed like the city. Live web research was unavailable in this run, so confidence is limited."}}